Summary: winemac: load plugin libraries named in WINEMAC_PLUGINS or the Plugins value before Cocoa starts
Category: system
Kind: feature
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c, macdrv_init(); written for
    wine-mac-builds after Second Chance's weak-dylib load command patched into
    winemac.so.
Upstream: no
Why: An app that embeds Wine may need code of its own inside the Mac driver
 (Objective-C hooks on Wine's windows, say). Without a hook it has to add a
 load command to winemac.so and re-sign it. Now macdrv_init dlopens each
 path in the WINEMAC_PLUGINS environment variable (inherited by child
 processes) and then in the Mac Driver "Plugins" registry value
 (HKCU\Software\Wine\Mac Driver, or the per-app AppDefaults key), each a
 colon-separated list, after reading the options and before Cocoa starts.
 A path that doesn't load is logged (err:macdrv) and skipped. With neither
 set nothing changes.
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine): had to patch a load
 command into winemac.so and re-sign it to load its in-process helpers
Uncertain: whether a plugin needs to load earlier (before setup_options) or
 later (after Cocoa starts); the brief asked for between the two.
Status: 2026-11-18 in a quick build of macfixes 11.22 (VM, not for release;
 smoke and the host OpenGL tests pass). On meeka (macOS 26.7, GUI session):
 WINEMAC_PLUGINS loads the plugin (in every process that starts the driver),
 a missing path is logged as err:macdrv and skipped, the Plugins value
 loads it, nothing loads with neither set. winemac-plugins passes on it and
 fails on 11.22-build8. In 11.22-build9 (CI, compiler cache on): the
 suite passes, winemac-plugins included (in the build VM). On meeka, an app
 that embeds Wine loaded its in-process helpers through WINEMAC_PLUGINS with
 winemac.so unpatched, and four games (White Wolf CD, Iji, Bioscopia, a Big
 Fish trial) ran with every helper armed, in bfgclient.exe as well.

